-- title:
--   Residue degree p-1 over the floor for Gauss valuation rings
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and $M\ge 5$ with $p\nmid M$, and let $L$ be a characteristic-zero field which is a $p$-th cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$, with $\zeta\in L$ a primitive $p$-th root of unity. Let $K$ be the $L$-subfield of $L((q))$ obtained by adjoining to $L$ the coefficientwise images (under [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81)) of the $q$-expansion field of level $\Gamma_1(Mp)$, i.e. of $\mathbb{Q}$ adjoined the ratios of integral forms for $\Gamma_1(Mp)$; let $K_1$ be the corresponding subfield built from $\Gamma_1(M)\cap\Gamma_0(p)$, with $K_1\le K$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation ring with fraction field $L$ whose maximal ideal contains $p$ and generated by $\varpi$, with $\zeta$ in the image of $A$, together with compatible $A$-algebra structures on $K$ and on $K_1$. Let $j\in K$ and $j_1\in K_1$ be nonzero elements whose Laurent expansions are the image of [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157). Let $W_0$ be a valuation subring of $K$ consisting exactly of those $f$ admitting a Gauss presentation over $A$: there are power series $x,y$ over $A$ with $y$ having nonzero reduction modulo the maximal ideal and $f\,y=x$ in $L((q))$; let $V$ be the valuation subring of $K_1$ that is the preimage of $W_0$. Given algebra structures $V\to W_0$ and on residue fields compatible with these inclusions and with reduction, the conclusion is that the residue field of $W_0$ has rank $p-1$ as a module over the residue field of $V$.
--
--   This computes the residue degree of the Gauss (Igusa) branch of $X_1(Mp)$ in characteristic $p$ over the corresponding branch on the floor $X(\Gamma_1(M)\cap\Gamma_0(p))$, the residue extension being that of the Igusa function field of level $M$ over the $q$-expansion field of $X_1(M)$ in characteristic $p$. Together with $[K:K_1]=p-1$ it feeds the fundamental inequality argument showing that exactly one valuation ring of $K$ lies above $V$, as used in [`ModularCurve.XOneP.eq_of_comap_inclusion_eq_comap_inclusion_of_gaussPresentation_x1_mul_x1x0`](thm.html#ModularCurve.XOneP.eq_of_comap_inclusion_eq_comap_inclusion_of_gaussPresentation_x1_mul_x1x0).
